('The angle of incidence equals the angle of reflection. This is the law of', 'Refraction', 'Reflection', 'Diffraction', 'Polarization', 'option2', 'The law of reflection states $\angle i = \angle r$, measured from the normal to the surface.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A concave mirror has its reflecting surface on the', 'Outer side of the sphere', 'Inner (cave) side of the sphere', 'Flat side', 'Both sides equally', 'option2', 'Concave means curved inward — the reflecting surface is on the inner side of the spherical segment.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The focal length of a spherical mirror of radius of curvature $R$ is', '$R$', '$2R$', '$R/2$', '$R/4$', 'option3', '$f = R/2$ for spherical mirrors (valid in the paraxial approximation).', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('An object placed at the centre of curvature of a concave mirror forms an image that is', 'At infinity', 'At the focus', 'At the centre of curvature, real and inverted, same size', 'Virtual and erect', 'option3', 'At $C$ ($u = -R = -2f$): $v = -2f$. Image is at $C$, real, inverted, same size.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The mirror formula relating object distance $u$, image distance $v$, and focal length $f$ is', '$1/v - 1/u = 1/f$', '$1/v + 1/u = 1/f$', '$v + u = f$', '$uv = f$', 'option2', 'Mirror formula: $1/v + 1/u = 1/f$ (with appropriate sign convention).', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A convex mirror always forms an image that is', 'Real and magnified', 'Virtual, erect, and diminished', 'Real and inverted', 'Virtual and magnified', 'option2', 'A convex mirror always produces a virtual, erect, diminished image regardless of object position.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The magnification produced by a mirror is given by $m = -v/u$. For a real inverted image, $m$ is', 'Positive', 'Negative', 'Zero', 'Infinite', 'option2', 'For a real inverted image: $v$ is negative (same side as object for concave), $u$ is negative. $m = -v/u < 0$ (negative means inverted).', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('An object is placed $30\;\text{cm}$ from a concave mirror of focal length $20\;\text{cm}$. The image distance is', '$-60\;\text{cm}$', '$+60\;\text{cm}$', '$-30\;\text{cm}$', '$+30\;\text{cm}$', 'option1', '$1/v + 1/(-30) = 1/(-20)$. $1/v = -1/20 + 1/30 = (-3+2)/60 = -1/60$. $v = -60\;\text{cm}$ (real, on same side as object).', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A concave mirror produces a $3\times$ magnified real image. If the object is at $20\;\text{cm}$, the focal length is', '$10\;\text{cm}$', '$15\;\text{cm}$', '$20\;\text{cm}$', '$30\;\text{cm}$', 'option2', 'Real image: $m = -v/u = -3$, so $v = 3u = -60\;\text{cm}$. $1/f = 1/(-60) + 1/(-20) = -4/60$. $f = -15\;\text{cm}$ (magnitude $15\;\text{cm}$).', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A convex mirror of focal length $15\;\text{cm}$ has an object at $30\;\text{cm}$. The image distance is', '$+10\;\text{cm}$', '$-10\;\text{cm}$', '$+30\;\text{cm}$', '$+15\;\text{cm}$', 'option1', '$1/v + 1/(-30) = 1/(+15)$. $1/v = 1/15 + 1/30 = 3/30 = 1/10$. $v = +10\;\text{cm}$ (virtual, behind mirror).', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The minimum length of a plane mirror for a person of height $h$ to see their full image is', '$h/2$', '$h$', '$h/3$', '$2h$', 'option1', 'By geometry, the mirror needs to span from midpoint of eyes-to-feet to midpoint of eyes-to-top-of-head, which is $h/2$.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Two plane mirrors are inclined at $60°$. The number of images of an object placed between them is', '$5$', '$6$', '$4$', '$3$', 'option1', 'Number of images $= 360°/\theta - 1 = 360/60 - 1 = 5$.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A concave mirror of focal length $f$ produces a virtual image when the object is placed', 'Beyond the centre of curvature', 'At the focus', 'Between the pole and the focus', 'At the centre of curvature', 'option3', 'When the object is between $P$ and $F$ ($|u| < |f|$), the concave mirror forms a virtual, erect, magnified image behind the mirror.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('An object moves from infinity towards a concave mirror of focal length $f$. The image moves from', 'Infinity towards $f$', '$f$ towards infinity (away from mirror)', '$f$ towards the pole', 'The pole towards $f$', 'option2', 'As object moves from $\infty$ to $F$: image moves from $F$ to $\infty$ (real side). Then for $u$ between $F$ and $P$: virtual image behind mirror.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A point object is placed at $15\;\text{cm}$ from a concave mirror of focal length $10\;\text{cm}$. The object starts moving towards the mirror at $4\;\text{cm/s}$. The speed of the image when the object is at $15\;\text{cm}$ is', '$36\;\text{cm/s}$', '$4\;\text{cm/s}$', '$8\;\text{cm/s}$', '$16\;\text{cm/s}$', 'option4', 'At $u = -15$, $f = -10$: $v = uf/(u-f) = (-15)(-10)/(-15+10) = 150/(-5) = -30$. $m = -v/u = -2$. Speed of image $= m^2 \times$ speed of object $= 4 \times 4 = 16\;\text{cm/s}$ (using $dv/dt = (v/u)^2 \times du/dt$).', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A concave mirror of focal length $20\;\text{cm}$ produces an image of the same size as the object. The object distance is', '$60\;\text{cm}$', '$20\;\text{cm}$', '$10\;\text{cm}$', '$40\;\text{cm}$', 'option4', 'Same size real image: $|m| = 1$, so $|v| = |u|$. Object at $C$: $u = 2f = 40\;\text{cm}$.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A thin rod of length $5\;\text{cm}$ is placed along the axis of a concave mirror of focal length $10\;\text{cm}$ with its near end at $15\;\text{cm}$. The length of the image is', '$15\;\text{cm}$', '$20\;\text{cm}$', '$5\;\text{cm}$', '$10\;\text{cm}$', 'option4', 'Near end at $u_1 = -15$: $v_1 = (-15)(-10)/(-15+10) = -30\;\text{cm}$. Far end at $u_2 = -20$: $v_2 = (-20)(-10)/(-20+10) = -20\;\text{cm}$. Image length $= |{-30} - ({-20})| = 10\;\text{cm}$.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A convex mirror is used as a rear-view mirror in vehicles because it', 'Provides a wider field of view and always forms erect images', 'Magnifies objects', 'Forms real images', 'Has longer focal length', 'option1', 'Convex mirrors give a diminished, erect, virtual image with a wider field of view, ideal for rear-view mirrors.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('An object is placed between two parallel plane mirrors. The brightest images are the', 'All equally bright', 'Last images', 'First few images (brightness decreases with each reflection)', 'Middle images', 'option3', 'Each reflection loses some light (no mirror is 100% reflective), so successive images get progressively dimmer.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A concave mirror of focal length $f$ is used to focus sunlight. The image of the Sun is formed at', 'The centre of curvature', 'The focus of the mirror', 'Infinity', 'The pole', 'option2', 'Sunlight is effectively from infinity. Parallel rays converge at the focus after reflection.', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The image formed by a concave mirror is real, inverted, and $4$ times the size of the object. If the image is at $80\;\text{cm}$ from the mirror, the focal length is', '$16\;\text{cm}$', '$20\;\text{cm}$', '$64\;\text{cm}$', '$32\;\text{cm}$', 'option1', '$m = -v/u = -4$ (real, inverted). $v = -80$, so $u = v/4 = -20\;\text{cm}$. $1/f = 1/(-80) + 1/(-20) = -1/80 - 4/80 = -5/80 = -1/16$. $f = -16\;\text{cm}$ (magnitude $16\;\text{cm}$).', 'p_reflection_mirrors', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),

