-- p_logic_gates (7 easy, 7 medium, 7 hard = 21)
-- ============================================================
('The output of an AND gate is HIGH only when', 'All inputs are LOW', 'Any input is HIGH', 'All inputs are HIGH', 'Any input is LOW', 'option3', 'AND: $Y = A \cdot B$. Output is 1 only when both $A = 1$ and $B = 1$.', 'p_logic_gates', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The output of an OR gate is HIGH when', 'All inputs are LOW', 'At least one input is HIGH', 'All inputs are HIGH only', 'No inputs are connected', 'option2', 'OR: $Y = A + B$. Output is 1 when at least one input is 1.', 'p_logic_gates', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A NOT gate', 'Has no output', 'Adds two inputs', 'Multiplies two inputs', 'Inverts the input', 'option4', 'NOT: $Y = \bar{A}$. If input is 0, output is 1 and vice versa.', 'p_logic_gates', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A NAND gate is equivalent to', 'Two OR gates', 'An OR gate followed by a NOT gate', 'A NOT gate followed by an AND gate', 'An AND gate followed by a NOT gate', 'option4', 'NAND: $Y = \overline{A \cdot B}$. It is AND + NOT.', 'p_logic_gates', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A NOR gate is equivalent to', 'An AND gate followed by a NOT gate', 'An OR gate followed by a NOT gate', 'A NOT gate followed by an OR gate', 'Two AND gates', 'option2', 'NOR: $Y = \overline{A + B}$. It is OR + NOT.', 'p_logic_gates', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The NAND gate is called a universal gate because', 'Any logic gate can be constructed using only NAND gates', 'It is the most common gate', 'It has the simplest circuit', 'It uses the least power', 'option1', 'NAND (and NOR) are universal — AND, OR, NOT can all be built from NAND gates alone.', 'p_logic_gates', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The Boolean expression for an XOR (exclusive OR) gate is', '$Y = \overline{AB}$', '$Y = AB$', '$Y = A + B$', '$Y = A\bar{B} + \bar{A}B$', 'option4', 'XOR: output is 1 when inputs are different. $Y = A \oplus B = A\bar{B} + \bar{A}B$.', 'p_logic_gates', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The truth table output for NAND with inputs $A = 1$, $B = 0$ is', '$0$', '$1$', 'Undefined', '$A$', 'option2', 'NAND: $Y = \overline{A \cdot B} = \overline{1 \cdot 0} = \overline{0} = 1$.', 'p_logic_gates', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('To make a NOT gate from a NAND gate, you should', 'Use two NAND gates in series', 'Leave one input open', 'Connect output to input', 'Connect both inputs together', 'option4', 'NAND with tied inputs: $Y = \overline{A \cdot A} = \bar{A}$. This is a NOT gate.', 'p_logic_gates', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('De Morgan''s first theorem states that', '$\overline{A \cdot B} = \bar{A} + \bar{B}$', '$\overline{A + B} = \bar{A} \cdot \bar{B}$', '$A + B = \bar{A} \cdot \bar{B}$', '$\overline{A + B} = A \cdot B$', 'option2', 'De Morgan I: $\overline{A + B} = \bar{A} \cdot \bar{B}$ (NOR = AND of complements).', 'p_logic_gates', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('De Morgan''s second theorem states that', '$\overline{A + B} = \bar{A} \cdot \bar{B}$', '$\overline{A \cdot B} = \bar{A} + \bar{B}$', '$A \cdot B = \bar{A} + \bar{B}$', '$\overline{A \cdot B} = A + B$', 'option2', 'De Morgan II: $\overline{A \cdot B} = \bar{A} + \bar{B}$ (NAND = OR of complements).', 'p_logic_gates', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The output of the combination NOT(A AND B) OR (A AND B) is always', '$0$', '$1$', '$A$', '$B$', 'option2', '$Y = \overline{AB} + AB$. For any values of $A$ and $B$: if $AB = 1$, $Y = 0 + 1 = 1$. If $AB = 0$, $Y = 1 + 0 = 1$. Always 1.', 'p_logic_gates', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('An AND gate can be made from NAND gates by', 'Connecting a NAND gate followed by a NOT (another NAND with tied inputs)', 'Using a single NAND gate', 'Connecting two NAND gates in parallel', 'It cannot be done', 'option1', 'AND from NAND: $Y = \overline{\overline{AB}} = AB$. Two NAND gates: first gives $\overline{AB}$, second (as NOT) gives $AB$.', 'p_logic_gates', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The Boolean expression $Y = \bar{A}B + A\bar{B} + AB$ simplifies to', '$\overline{A + B}$', '$AB$', '$A \oplus B$', '$A + B$', 'option4', '$Y = \bar{A}B + A(\bar{B} + B) = \bar{A}B + A = A + B$ (by absorption: $A + \bar{A}B = A + B$).', 'p_logic_gates', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The number of rows in a truth table for a 3-input gate is', '$6$', '$8$', '$3$', '$9$', 'option2', 'For $n$ inputs: $2^n$ rows. For $n = 3$: $2^3 = 8$ rows.', 'p_logic_gates', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The Boolean expression $Y = AB + A\bar{B}$ simplifies to', '$A$', '$B$', '$A + B$', '$AB$', 'option1', '$Y = A(B + \bar{B}) = A \cdot 1 = A$.', 'p_logic_gates', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('An XOR gate can be built using', '4 NAND gates', '2 NAND gates', '1 NAND gate', '6 NAND gates', 'option1', 'XOR from NAND gates requires 4 NAND gates in a specific configuration.', 'p_logic_gates', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The output of cascading two NOT gates is', 'Same as the input', 'Complement of input', 'Always 0', 'Always 1', 'option1', '$Y = \overline{\bar{A}} = A$. Double negation returns the original.', 'p_logic_gates', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A half-adder circuit uses', 'A NAND and a NOR gate', 'Two OR gates', 'An XOR gate and an AND gate', 'Three AND gates', 'option3', 'Half-adder: Sum $= A \oplus B$ (XOR), Carry $= AB$ (AND).', 'p_logic_gates', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The Boolean expression $\overline{\bar{A} + \bar{B}}$ equals', '$\overline{AB}$', '$A + B$', '$\bar{A}\bar{B}$', '$AB$', 'option4', 'By De Morgan: $\overline{\bar{A} + \bar{B}} = \overline{\bar{A}} \cdot \overline{\bar{B}} = A \cdot B = AB$.', 'p_logic_gates', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The minimum number of NAND gates required to implement an OR gate is', '$3$', '$2$', '$4$', '$1$', 'option1', 'OR from NAND: first NOT $A$ (1 NAND), then NOT $B$ (1 NAND), then NAND($\bar{A}$, $\bar{B}$) = $\overline{\bar{A}\bar{B}} = A + B$ (1 NAND). Total: 3.', 'p_logic_gates', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),

