('The least count of a Vernier caliper with main scale division $1\;\text{mm}$ and $50$ Vernier divisions matching $49$ main scale divisions is', '$0.5\;\text{mm}$', '$0.1\;\text{mm}$', '$0.01\;\text{mm}$', '$0.02\;\text{mm}$', 'option4', 'LC $= 1\;\text{MSD} - 1\;\text{VSD} = 1 - 49/50 = 1/50 = 0.02\;\text{mm}$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The least count of a screw gauge with pitch $0.5\;\text{mm}$ and $50$ divisions on the circular scale is', '$0.01\;\text{mm}$', '$0.1\;\text{mm}$', '$0.001\;\text{mm}$', '$0.5\;\text{mm}$', 'option1', 'LC $= \text{pitch}/\text{divisions} = 0.5/50 = 0.01\;\text{mm}$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Zero error in a screw gauge occurs when', 'The zero of the circular scale does not coincide with the reference line when jaws are closed', 'The screw is broken', 'The pitch is wrong', 'The thimble is missing', 'option1', 'Zero error must be noted and corrected: positive (subtract) or negative (add) from readings.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The time period of a simple pendulum depends on', 'Amplitude (for large angles)', 'Mass of the bob', 'Length and acceleration due to gravity', 'Material of the string', 'option3', '$T = 2\pi\sqrt{L/g}$ (for small amplitudes). Independent of mass and amplitude.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In a simple pendulum experiment, the time for $20$ oscillations is measured to reduce', 'Random error in the time period', 'Systematic error', 'Zero error', 'Parallax error', 'option1', 'Measuring multiple oscillations and dividing reduces the percentage random error in the period.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Young''s modulus can be determined experimentally using', 'A spectrometer', 'A calorimeter', 'A potentiometer', 'Searle''s apparatus', 'option4', 'Searle''s apparatus measures the extension of a wire under load to determine $Y = FL/(A\Delta L)$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A metre scale can measure lengths with an accuracy of', '$0.1\;\text{mm}$', '$1\;\text{mm}$', '$0.01\;\text{mm}$', '$1\;\text{cm}$', 'option2', 'The smallest division on a metre scale is $1\;\text{mm}$, so the least count is $1\;\text{mm}$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A Vernier caliper reads $3.2\;\text{cm}$ on the main scale and the $6$th Vernier division coincides. If LC $= 0.02\;\text{mm}$, the reading is', '$3.32\;\text{cm}$', '$3.26\;\text{cm}$', '$3.206\;\text{cm}$', '$3.212\;\text{cm}$', 'option4', 'Reading $= 3.2 + 6 \times 0.002 = 3.2 + 0.012 = 3.212\;\text{cm}$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In a simple pendulum experiment, if the length is increased by $4$ times, the time period', 'Doubles', 'Quadruples', 'Halves', 'Remains the same', 'option1', '$T \propto \sqrt{L}$. If $L \to 4L$: $T \to 2T$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The percentage error in $g$ determined from $T = 2\pi\sqrt{L/g}$ if $\Delta L/L = 1\%$ and $\Delta T/T = 2\%$ is', '$5\%$', '$3\%$', '$4\%$', '$1\%$', 'option1', '$g = 4\pi^2 L/T^2$. $\Delta g/g = \Delta L/L + 2\Delta T/T = 1 + 4 = 5\%$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A screw gauge has a positive zero error of $3$ divisions (LC $= 0.01\;\text{mm}$). The correction to be applied is', 'Subtract $0.03\;\text{mm}$', 'Add $0.03\;\text{mm}$', 'Subtract $0.3\;\text{mm}$', 'Add $0.3\;\text{mm}$', 'option1', 'Positive zero error: the instrument reads more than actual. Subtract $3 \times 0.01 = 0.03\;\text{mm}$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In Searle''s experiment, the reference wire is used to', 'Provide the extension', 'Measure the load', 'Compensate for temperature changes and support sagging', 'Act as a spring', 'option3', 'The reference wire eliminates errors due to thermal expansion and yielding of the support.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Backlash error in a screw gauge is caused by', 'Zero error', 'Wear in the screw threads creating play', 'Parallax', 'Temperature changes', 'option2', 'Backlash: loose fit between screw and nut. Avoided by always rotating the thimble in one direction.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Parallax error in reading a scale is eliminated by', 'Using a magnifying glass', 'Keeping the eye directly above the reading', 'Using a thicker scale', 'Reading from an angle', 'option2', 'Parallax is eliminated by ensuring the line of sight is perpendicular to the scale.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In a simple pendulum experiment, the effective length includes', 'The string length minus the bob radius', 'Only the string length', 'Only the bob radius', 'The length of the string plus the radius of the bob', 'option4', 'Effective length $= $ string length $+$ radius of bob (distance from pivot to centre of mass of bob).', 'p_exp_mechanics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In Searle''s experiment for Young''s modulus, the graph of extension vs load is', 'An exponential curve', 'A parabola', 'A straight line through the origin (within elastic limit)', 'A horizontal line', 'option3', 'Within the elastic limit, extension $\propto$ load (Hooke''s law). The slope gives $L/(AY)$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The time period of a simple pendulum on the Moon (where $g_{Moon} = g/6$) compared to Earth is', '$\sqrt{6}$ times shorter', '$6$ times longer', '$\sqrt{6}$ times longer', 'The same', 'option3', '$T \propto 1/\sqrt{g}$. $T_{Moon}/T_{Earth} = \sqrt{g/g_{Moon}} = \sqrt{6}$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('If the diameter of a wire is measured as $d = 1.25 \pm 0.01\;\text{mm}$, the percentage error in the cross-sectional area is', '$1.6\%$', '$0.8\%$', '$3.2\%$', '$0.4\%$', 'option1', '$A = \pi d^2/4$. $\Delta A/A = 2\Delta d/d = 2 \times 0.01/1.25 = 0.016 = 1.6\%$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('A Vernier caliper has $20$ divisions on the Vernier scale matching $19$ main scale divisions (MSD $= 1\;\text{mm}$). The least count is', '$0.5\;\text{mm}$', '$0.02\;\text{mm}$', '$0.1\;\text{mm}$', '$0.05\;\text{mm}$', 'option4', 'LC $= 1 - 19/20 = 1/20 = 0.05\;\text{mm}$.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In a pendulum experiment, the bob should be', 'Light and large', 'Heavy and small (to minimize air resistance and ensure point mass)', 'Any size', 'Hollow', 'option2', 'A heavy, small bob minimizes air drag and approximates a point mass at the end of the string.', 'p_exp_mechanics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),

