('In the falling sphere method, the viscosity of a liquid at higher temperature is expected to be', 'Lower (viscosity decreases with temperature for liquids)', 'Higher', 'The same', 'Unpredictable', 'option1', 'For liquids, viscosity decreases with increasing temperature as intermolecular forces weaken.', 'p_exp_fluids_heat', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The accuracy of the capillary rise method for surface tension is improved by', 'Heating the liquid', 'Using a wide tube', 'Using a narrow capillary and measuring the height carefully', 'Using a coloured liquid', 'option3', 'Narrower capillary gives larger rise (easier to measure) and reduces meniscus correction errors.', 'p_exp_fluids_heat', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
