-- p_exp_optics (7 easy, 7 medium, 7 hard = 21)
-- ============================================================
('The focal length of a convex lens can be determined by', 'The parallax method (u-v method)', 'A galvanometer', 'A potentiometer', 'A calorimeter', 'option1', 'Place object at various distances, find image position by parallax, plot $1/v$ vs $1/u$ to find $f$.', 'p_exp_optics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In the u-v method for finding focal length, the graph of $1/v$ vs $1/u$ is', 'A circle', 'A parabola', 'A hyperbola', 'A straight line', 'option4', '$1/v - 1/u = 1/f$. Plot of $1/v$ vs $1/u$ is linear with slope $1$ and intercepts $1/f$.', 'p_exp_optics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The angle of minimum deviation of a prism is measured using', 'A spectrometer', 'A microscope', 'A galvanometer', 'A potentiometer', 'option1', 'A spectrometer with a prism table measures the angle of minimum deviation by rotating the prism.', 'p_exp_optics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The refractive index of a prism can be determined from', 'The temperature of the prism', 'The colour of the prism', 'The weight of the prism', 'The angle of the prism and the angle of minimum deviation', 'option4', '$n = \sin((A + \delta_m)/2)/\sin(A/2)$.', 'p_exp_optics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Parallax is eliminated when', 'They move in opposite directions', 'The image and the object pin appear to move together (no relative shift)', 'They are far apart', 'The eye is closed', 'option2', 'No parallax means the image coincides with the pin — they move together when the eye is shifted.', 'p_exp_optics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In the spectrometer experiment, the telescope is first adjusted for', 'Parallel rays (focused at infinity)', 'Near objects', 'The prism', 'The collimator', 'option1', 'The telescope is focused at infinity (using a distant object) before the experiment begins.', 'p_exp_optics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The collimator in a spectrometer produces', 'A diverging beam', 'A converging beam', 'A parallel beam of light', 'Polarized light', 'option3', 'The collimator has a slit at the focus of its lens, producing parallel rays.', 'p_exp_optics', 1, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In the u-v method, the focal length of a convex lens is found to be $15\;\text{cm}$. If $u = -20\;\text{cm}$, the image distance $v$ is', '$+60\;\text{cm}$', '$-60\;\text{cm}$', '$+30\;\text{cm}$', '$-30\;\text{cm}$', 'option1', '$1/v = 1/f + 1/u = 1/15 + 1/(-20) = (4-3)/60 = 1/60$. $v = +60\;\text{cm}$.', 'p_exp_optics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The graph of $v$ vs $u$ for a convex lens is', 'A rectangular hyperbola', 'A straight line', 'A parabola', 'A circle', 'option1', 'From $1/v - 1/u = 1/f$: $v = uf/(u+f)$. This is a rectangular hyperbola in the $u$-$v$ plane.', 'p_exp_optics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In a spectrometer, the Schuster method is used to', 'Find the wavelength', 'Measure the prism angle', 'Calibrate the telescope', 'Adjust the prism for minimum deviation', 'option4', 'Schuster''s method: adjust the prism so that images on both sides of minimum deviation are equally sharp.', 'p_exp_optics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The angle of the prism in a spectrometer is measured by', 'Reflecting light from both faces and measuring the angle between reflected beams', 'Looking through the prism', 'Weighing the prism', 'Measuring its sides', 'option1', 'Prism angle $A = (180° - \theta)/1$ where $\theta$ is the angle between the two reflected images of the slit.', 'p_exp_optics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In the displacement method for focal length, a convex lens is moved between a fixed object and screen. The focal length is', '$f = (D^2 - d^2)/(4D)$ where $D$ is the object-screen distance and $d$ is the lens displacement', '$f = D/4$', '$f = d/4$', '$f = Dd/4$', 'option1', 'Two positions of the lens give sharp images. $f = (D^2 - d^2)/(4D)$.', 'p_exp_optics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The refractive index of a liquid can be found using', 'A convex lens and the liquid as a lens (or a hollow prism filled with liquid)', 'A galvanometer', 'A potentiometer', 'A screw gauge', 'option1', 'A hollow prism filled with liquid acts as a prism. Measure minimum deviation to find $n$.', 'p_exp_optics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In the u-v method, the minimum distance between object and real image for a convex lens is', '$f$', '$2f$', '$4f$', '$3f$', 'option3', 'Minimum distance $D_{min} = 4f$ (when $u = v = 2f$).', 'p_exp_optics', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In the displacement method, if $D = 60\;\text{cm}$ and $d = 20\;\text{cm}$, the focal length is', '$\approx 15\;\text{cm}$', '$\approx 13.3\;\text{cm}$', '$\approx 20\;\text{cm}$', '$\approx 10\;\text{cm}$', 'option2', '$f = (D^2 - d^2)/(4D) = (3600 - 400)/240 = 3200/240 = 13.3\;\text{cm}$.', 'p_exp_optics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The resolving power of a spectrometer depends on', 'The colour of light only', 'The brightness of the source', 'The size of the prism', 'The number of lines on the grating and the order of diffraction', 'option4', 'Resolving power $= mN$ for a grating, or $t(dn/d\lambda)$ for a prism.', 'p_exp_optics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In the i-$\delta$ curve for a prism, the curve is', 'U-shaped with a minimum at $\delta_m$', 'A straight line', 'An inverted U', 'A circle', 'option1', 'The deviation $\delta$ decreases as $i$ increases, reaches a minimum $\delta_m$, then increases again.', 'p_exp_optics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The Cauchy equation for dispersion is', '$n = A\lambda + B$', '$n = A + B/\lambda^2 + C/\lambda^4$', '$n = A + B\lambda$', '$n = A\lambda^2$', 'option2', 'Cauchy''s empirical formula: $n(\lambda) = A + B/\lambda^2 + C/\lambda^4 + ...$', 'p_exp_optics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('In the u-v method, systematic errors can be reduced by', 'Plotting $1/v$ vs $1/u$ and finding $f$ from the intercept', 'Taking a single reading', 'Using a very small lens', 'Ignoring parallax', 'option1', 'The graphical method averages out random errors and the intercept gives $1/f$ directly.', 'p_exp_optics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The angular dispersion of a prism is measured by', 'The difference in angles of minimum deviation for two wavelengths', 'The prism angle', 'The refractive index', 'The thickness of the prism', 'option1', 'Angular dispersion $= \delta_V - \delta_R$ (difference in deviation for violet and red light).', 'p_exp_optics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('The focal length of a concave mirror can be found by', 'The u-v method using parallax, or by focusing a distant object', 'A potentiometer', 'A galvanometer', 'A Wheatstone bridge', 'option1', 'For a distant object, the image forms at the focus. Alternatively, use the mirror formula with measured $u$ and $v$.', 'p_exp_optics', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),

